    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d712">

                <pb facs="0758" n="656" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg656"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/5834: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-11-29T16:00:00+08:00">November 29, 1933—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 29—8 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>885. Department’s 383, November 23, 7 p.m. British Legation has agreed informally
                    to revision of draft suggested by the Department in its telegram under
                    reference. Objectionable clause has been deleted and the words “above quoted”
                    have been changed to “above cited”. May I initial the revised memorandum?<anchor
                        n="32" xml:id="d712-f1"/></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d712-f1" n="32" xml:id="d712-f1-content">
                <p>The Department authorized the request by telegram No. 384, November 29, The joint
                    memorandum was dated December 20.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
